WEBVTT

00:00.420 --> 00:04.780
We're asked to identify the
percent, amount, and base in

00:04.780 --> 00:05.640
this problem.

00:05.640 --> 00:11.320
And they ask us, 150 is
25% of what number?

00:11.320 --> 00:13.650
They don't ask us to solve it,
but it's too tempting.

00:13.650 --> 00:16.800
So what I want to do is first
answer this question that

00:16.800 --> 00:18.390
they're not even asking
us to solve.

00:18.390 --> 00:20.140
But first, I want to answer
this question.

00:20.140 --> 00:23.090
And then we can think about what
the percent, the amount,

00:23.090 --> 00:25.620
and the base is, because
those are just words.

00:25.620 --> 00:26.680
Those are just definitions.

00:26.680 --> 00:28.330
The important thing is
to be able to solve a

00:28.330 --> 00:29.620
problem like this.

00:29.620 --> 00:36.640
So they're saying 150 is
25% of what number?

00:36.640 --> 00:44.030
Or another way to view this,
150 is 25% of some number.

00:44.030 --> 00:52.690
So let's let x, x is equal
to the number that

00:52.690 --> 00:58.080
150 is 25% of, right?

00:58.080 --> 00:59.150
That's what we need
to figure out.

00:59.150 --> 01:01.470
150 is 25% of what number?

01:01.470 --> 01:03.920
That number right here
we're seeing is x.

01:03.920 --> 01:07.270
So that tells us that if we
start with x, and if we were

01:07.270 --> 01:16.790
to take 25% of x, you could
imagine, that's the same thing

01:16.790 --> 01:21.500
as multiplying it by 25%, which
is the same thing as

01:21.500 --> 01:23.420
multiplying it, if you
view it as a decimal,

01:23.420 --> 01:27.920
times 0.25 times x.

01:27.920 --> 01:29.230
These two statements
are identical.

01:29.230 --> 01:32.290
So if you start with that
number, you take 25% of it, or

01:32.290 --> 01:41.870
you multiply it by 0.25, that
is going to be equal to 150.

01:41.870 --> 01:45.780
150 is 25% of this number.

01:45.780 --> 01:48.760
And then you can solve for x.

01:48.760 --> 01:52.280
So let's just start with
this one over here.

01:52.280 --> 01:54.110
Let me just write it separately,
so you understand

01:54.110 --> 01:54.780
what I'm doing.

01:54.780 --> 02:01.190
0.25 times some number
is equal to 150.

02:01.190 --> 02:02.910
Now there's two ways
we can do this.

02:02.910 --> 02:07.780
We can divide both sides of this
equation by 0.25, or if

02:07.780 --> 02:10.930
you recognize that four quarters
make a dollar, you

02:10.930 --> 02:14.230
could say, let's multiply both
sides of this equation by 4.

02:14.230 --> 02:15.200
You could do either one.

02:15.200 --> 02:17.550
I'll do the first, because
that's how we normally do

02:17.550 --> 02:20.370
algebra problems like this.

02:20.370 --> 02:28.590
So let's just multiply
both by 0.25.

02:28.590 --> 02:30.050
That will just be an x.

02:30.050 --> 02:35.040
And then the right-hand side
will be 150 divided by 0.25.

02:35.040 --> 02:36.790
And the reason why I wanted to
is really it's just good

02:36.790 --> 02:38.420
practice dividing
by a decimal.

02:38.420 --> 02:39.620
So let's do that.

02:39.620 --> 02:46.090
So we want to figure out what
150 divided by 0.25 is.

02:46.090 --> 02:47.610
And we've done this before.

02:47.610 --> 02:49.590
When you divide by a decimal,
what you can do is you can

02:49.590 --> 02:51.950
make the number that you're
dividing into the other

02:51.950 --> 02:54.660
number, you can turn this into
a whole number by essentially

02:54.660 --> 02:56.980
shifting the decimal
two to the right.

02:56.980 --> 02:58.715
But if you do that for the
number in the denominator, you

02:58.715 --> 03:00.700
also have to do that
to the numerator.

03:00.700 --> 03:04.150
So right now you can view
this as 150.00.

03:04.150 --> 03:07.360
If you multiply 0.25 times
100, you're shifting the

03:07.360 --> 03:09.070
decimal two to the right.

03:09.070 --> 03:11.220
Then you'd also have to do
that with 150, so then it

03:11.220 --> 03:13.290
becomes 15,000.

03:13.290 --> 03:15.250
Shift it two to the right.

03:15.250 --> 03:17.470
So our decimal place
becomes like this.

03:17.470 --> 03:20.510
So 150 divided by 0.25
is the same thing as

03:20.510 --> 03:23.840
15,000 divided by 25.

03:23.840 --> 03:26.520
And let's just work it
out really fast.

03:26.520 --> 03:31.960
So 25 doesn't go into 1, doesn't
go into 15, it goes

03:31.960 --> 03:34.650
into 150, what is that?

03:34.650 --> 03:36.020
Six times, right?

03:36.020 --> 03:37.890
If it goes into 100 four
times, then it goes

03:37.890 --> 03:41.290
into 150 six times.

03:41.290 --> 03:45.290
6 times 0.25 is-- or actually,
this is now a 25.

03:45.290 --> 03:46.170
We've shifted the decimal.

03:46.170 --> 03:47.920
This decimal is sitting
right over there.

03:47.920 --> 03:50.990
So 6 times 25 is 150.

03:50.990 --> 03:52.190
You subtract.

03:52.190 --> 03:53.270
You get no remainder.

03:53.270 --> 03:55.390
Bring down this 0 right here.

03:55.390 --> 03:58.180
25 goes into 0 zero times.

03:58.180 --> 03:59.990
0 times 25 is 0.

03:59.990 --> 04:00.810
Subtract.

04:00.810 --> 04:01.640
No remainder.

04:01.640 --> 04:03.620
Bring down this last 0.

04:03.620 --> 04:06.140
25 goes into 0 zero times.

04:06.140 --> 04:07.710
0 times 25 is 0.

04:07.710 --> 04:08.440
Subtract.

04:08.440 --> 04:09.640
No remainder.

04:09.640 --> 04:13.840
So 150 divided by 0.25
is equal to 600.

04:13.840 --> 04:15.470
And you might have been able
to do that in your head,

04:15.470 --> 04:20.220
because when we were at this
point in our equation, 0.25x

04:20.220 --> 04:23.790
is equal to 150, you could
have just multiplied both

04:23.790 --> 04:25.750
sides of this equation
times 4.

04:25.750 --> 04:29.170
4 times 0.25 is the same
thing as 4 times

04:29.170 --> 04:31.190
1/4, which is a whole.

04:31.190 --> 04:33.860
And 4 times 150 is 600.

04:33.860 --> 04:35.790
So you would have gotten
it either way.

04:35.790 --> 04:38.390
And this makes total sense.

04:38.390 --> 04:43.710
If 150 is 25% of some number,
that means 150 should be 1/4

04:43.710 --> 04:44.310
of that number.

04:44.310 --> 04:46.690
It should be a lot smaller than
that number, and it is.

04:46.690 --> 04:49.710
150 is 1/4 of 600.

04:49.710 --> 04:52.070
Now let's answer their
actual question.

04:52.070 --> 04:55.950
Identify the percent.

04:55.950 --> 05:00.800
Well, that looks like 25%,
that's the percent.

05:00.800 --> 05:03.820
The amount and the base
in this problem.

05:03.820 --> 05:05.990
And based on how they're wording
it, I assume amount

05:05.990 --> 05:10.330
means when you take the 25% of
the base, so they're saying

05:10.330 --> 05:14.335
that the amount-- as my best
sense of it-- is that the

05:14.335 --> 05:24.540
amount is equal to the percent
times the base.

05:24.540 --> 05:27.130
Let me do the base in green.

05:27.130 --> 05:29.410
So the base is the number you're
taking the percent of.

05:29.410 --> 05:32.650
The amount is the quantity
that that percentage

05:32.650 --> 05:33.610
represents.

05:33.610 --> 05:39.670
So here we already saw
the percent is 25%.

05:39.670 --> 05:40.960
That's the percent.

05:40.960 --> 05:52.910
The number that we're taking
25% of, or the base, is x.

05:52.910 --> 05:54.620
The value of it is 600.

05:54.620 --> 05:55.680
We figured it out.

05:55.680 --> 05:59.180
And the amount is 150.

05:59.180 --> 06:01.980
This right here is the amount.

06:01.980 --> 06:03.350
The amount is 150.

06:03.350 --> 06:07.630
150 is 25% of the
base, of 600.

06:07.630 --> 06:10.610
The important thing is how
you solve this problem.

06:10.610 --> 06:13.950
The words themselves, you know,
those are all really

06:13.950 --> 06:15.460
just definitions.
